{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\np='draft/epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\t\t\\\"owner_instance_status_after\\\": int(owner.r.InstanceSpace[0][0].Status),\n\t\t\\\"owner_cmd_op_after\\\": cmdOp(owner.r.InstanceSpace[0][0].Cmds)})''',\n'''\t\t\\\"owner_instance_status_after\\\": int(owner.r.InstanceSpace[0][0].Status),\n\t\t\\\"owner_cmds_len\\\": len(owner.r.InstanceSpace[0][0].Cmds),\n\t\t\\\"owner_cmd_op_after\\\": cmdOp(owner.r.InstanceSpace[0][0].Cmds)})''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncp draft/epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go draft/scratch/epaxos/ && cd draft/scratch && timeout 120 go test -run 'TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoverySameBallotOrder' -count=1 -v ./epaxos 2>&1 | grep -cE 'owner_cmds_len'; cd - >/dev/null\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nexp={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@rec-same-ballot-tiebreak\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\\\"execution_package\\\":\\\"./epaxos\\\",\n \\\"test_names\\\":[\\\"TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoverySameBallotOrder\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[{\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1127,\\\"end_line\\\":1141},\n            {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1204,\\\"end_line\\\":1235}],\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-prepare-reply-adopt\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\",\\\"s-preaccept-guard\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Owner replica 0 proposes X on its own instance (0,0), replica 1's non-equal pre-accept reply is delivered and replica 1 then fails, so the owner enters the Accept phase at ballot 0 towards replicas 2 and 3; replica 3 accepts without ever pre-accepting (its state holds no command), and the owner's AcceptReplies are left in flight. The owner, alive and still holding X, then runs startRecoveryForInstance(0,0); the harness delivers the Prepare replies of replicas 2, 3 and 4 in a chosen order (replica 2 carries X at value ballot 0, replicas 3 and 4 carry no command at the same ballot) and records whether the owner re-proposes a command and what its instance holds afterwards. The test runs the same message set twice with the empty reply last in one run and first in the other.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Same construction, transport boundary and crash model as the other experiments in this harness.\\\",\n   \\\"Delivery order among the prepare replies is chosen by the harness, which is what a real network does not fix; the read order is not altered.\\\",\n   \\\"No production logic is modified.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No client path, no state-machine execution, no run() loop or recovery timer loop.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"n\\\":5,\\\"f\\\":2,\\\"owner\\\":0,\\\"value_ballot\\\":0,\\\"tie_replies\\\":[2,3,4],\\\"orders\\\":[\\\"2,4,3\\\",\\\"3,4,2\\\"]}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness drives the owner's proposal and accept phase through the target's own handlers, fails replica 1 after its reply, delivers the Accept to replicas 2 and 3, then calls the owner's startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) and delivers each collected PrepareReply to the owner, recording the owner's leader-bookkeeping state (status, appended count, nacks, prepared flag) and the instance's command length before and after the dispatch.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A recovery of an instance must not drop the instance's command when a reply without a command arrives at the same value ballot as replies that carry one, and the adopted value must not depend on the delivery order of equally admissible replies.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The 